<p>US federal prosecutors said Shamim Mafi, a 44-year-old Iranian national and lawful permanent resident living in Woodland Hills, California, was arrested at Los Angeles International Airport on Saturday night and charged with brokering arms sales from Iran to Sudan without legal authorization. Authorities say she arranged the sale of drones, bombs, bomb fuses, and millions of rounds of ammunition made in Iran for the Sudanese Armed Forces. The case draws wider attention to Sudan’s war and to alleged Iranian networks moving weapons into Africa. Prosecutors framed the arrest as an enforcement action against unlicensed arms dealing linked to Tehran, while published reporting included no public response from Mafi or Iranian officials at the time of publication.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/WwZnH0RePkLZLQazPbiKtjlIyrWKLAgRQuLEyuu-azTVlchr7EsQVBGi3CMHRtiCSxyXhPDUoCH2R_YoYgBvNcBINeLoxG3hu0-dfowFwA3sRWYscVekNZDlxau5tYC4wUhRDDfKGUV4HBBq6JERiGIpKMX28kpo99peRdqoZ8FkgoeR' alt='Los Angeles International Airport, where Shamim Mafi was arrested, according to reports.' /><br /><blockquote>Brokering the sale of drones, bombs, bomb fuses and millions of rounds of ammunition manufactured by Iran and sold to Sudan - Bill Essayli</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US Attorney Bill Essayli: Essayli announced the arrest in a social media post, making that public message one of the first ways the case reached a wider audience. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3350660/woman-charged-us-trafficking-arms-sudan-iranian-government'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3350660/woman-charged-us-trafficking-arms-sudan-iranian-government'>Los Angeles woman charged in US with trafficking arms to Sudan for Iran</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iranian-origin-businesswoman-shamim-mafi-allegedly-made-arms-deal-for-tehran-